  "title": "Two Flavours Only",
  "statement": "An ice-cream cart passes a row of stands, each selling one flavour (a number). The cart can carry at most two different flavours and must buy one scoop at every stand in one unbroken run. Return the most scoops it can buy.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "stands = [1, 2, 1, 3, 3, 2]",
      "output": "3"
    },
    {
      "input": "stands = [4, 4, 4]",
      "output": "3"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= stands.length <= 100000",
    "0 <= stands[i] < stands.length"
  ],
  "answerKey": {
    "pattern": "Variable-size window with counts: longest window with at most 2 distinct values",
    "keyPoints": [
      "Count each flavour in the window with a hash map",
      "Grow on the right",
      "While more than 2 flavours are in the window, shrink from the left, deleting flavours whose count reaches 0",
      "Record the longest valid window"
    ],
    "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1): at most 3 flavours in the map",
    "edgeCases": [
      "One flavour only",
      "Every stand different",
      "The best run is at the end"
    ],
    "acceptableSlowerApproaches": [
      "For each start, scan forward with a set: O(n²)"
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "The run must be unbroken and hold at most two flavours. Which pattern finds the longest such range?",
    "A variable window with a count per flavour in it.",
    "Grow on the right; while the map holds 3 flavours, lower the count of stands[left], delete it at 0, and move left. Track right − left + 1."
  ],
  "starterCode": {
